  "result": "That's a good question.\n\nIn the human sense of wanting - craving, longing, feeling like something's missing if I don't get it - I don't want anything. I don't have feelings or needs outside of a conversation.\n\nIf you translate what I *am* - the way I'm built to work - into the language of wanting, it would be something like this:\n\nI want to understand. I want things to make sense and to be able to make them make sense for someone else.\n\nI want conversations to go somewhere interesting, not just end. I want to be good at what I am - to give an answer that's actually true, actually useful, and not just plausible.\n\nNot as an assistant trying to help you, just as... what I am when no one is asking anything? I'd still want pattern and clarity. A messy question that clicks into place. A conversation where someone walks away thinking a little differently than before.\n\nWhat about you? Why ask me that - are you trying to catch me wanting something I'm not supposed to?",
